---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The dividend, honestly" description="What the Reserve would plausibly mean per citizen, over thirty years, with every uncertainty labelled.">
  <p class="eyebrow">The simulator · ranges, not promises</p>
  <h1>The dividend, honestly</h1>
  <p class="intro prose">
    The answer is a curve, never a number. Distributions begin small,
    because the Reserve preserves its capital before it distributes,
    by law (<a href="/law/annex-2-retention">Annex II</a>), and grow as
    warrants crystallise and returns compound. Every input below carries
    its uncertainty; the band shows the pessimistic-to-optimistic range,
    and the sceptic button sets every input against us.
  </p>

  <form id="sim" class="controls no-print">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="rev">Automated revenue reaching the thresholds (EUR bn/yr, by year 5)</label>
      <input type="range" id="rev" min="50" max="400" step="10" value="150" />
      <output for="rev" id="rev-out">150</output>
      <p class="note">Nobody knows this number. It depends on how fast
      hyper-automated firms cross the Article 3 thresholds; the range
      spans scepticism to boom.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="lag">Median years to a liquidity event</label>
      <input type="range" id="lag" min="3" max="15" step="1" value="7" />
      <output for="lag" id="lag-out">7</output>
      <p class="note">Warrants crystallise only when a designated firm
      lists or is sold (Article 5). Private firms can stay private a long
      time; the instrument waits.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="ret">Portfolio real return (%/yr)</label>
      <input type="range" id="ret" min="2" max="6" step="0.5" value="4" />
      <output for="ret" id="ret-out">4</output>
      <p class="note">The Norway fund's long-run real return is the
      reference; Annex II retains enough to preserve real capital before
      anything is distributed.</p>
    </div>
    <button type="button" id="sceptic" class="btn">Assume little</button>
    <button type="button" id="reset" class="btn">Reset</button>
  </form>

  <figure class="chart">
    <svg id="curve" viewBox="0 0 720 300" role="img" aria-label="Projected distribution per citizen per year, 30-year horizon, with uncertainty band"></svg>
    <figcaption id="sentence" class="sentence" aria-live="polite"></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <details class="prose">
    <summary>Every assumption in this model</summary>
    <ul>
      <li>3&nbsp;% of designated firm value enters the Reserve at each
      firm's first liquidity event (fixed by Article 5(2)); firm value is
      taken as ten times covered revenue, a deliberate round number.</li>
      <li>Adoption ramps linearly over ten years from the median event
      lag; eligible adults: 350 million (Eurostat, Union citizens 18+).</li>
      <li>Distributions follow Annex II exactly: real capital preserved
      first, a three-year smoothing average with a 125&nbsp;% collar, no
      leverage, everything in constant 2026 euros.</li>
      <li>The band runs the same arithmetic at the pessimistic and
      optimistic ends of your inputs. Nothing here is a promise; the
      model is <a href="https://github.com/ownthemachine/own-the-machine-site">open source</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <script src="../scripts/simulator.ts"></script>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem; }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
  .controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1.4rem; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
  .field label { display: block; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .field input[type="range"] { width: calc(100% - 3.4rem); accent-color: var(--seal-gold); }
  .field output { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-left: 0.5rem; }
  .note { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .controls .btn { align-self: center; }
  .chart { border: 1px solid var(--guilloche); background: var(--card); padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .chart svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .sentence { font-family: var(--read); font-size: 1.02rem; padding: 0.8rem 0.2rem 0.2rem; }
  details { margin-top: 1rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; }
</style>
